    end_line: 630
    content: "---\nname: \"gemini-api\"\ndescription: >-\n  MANDATORY for any task involving Gemini API integration in Android. Use when the user asks to use Gemini models, call Gemini API, or implement AI features. Covers model selection, REST API calls, Firebase AI, and security.\n---\n\n## Supported Models\n\nWhen an Agent selects a model, it **MUST** evaluate the rules in the following\nstrict priority order: (1) User-specified full model name, (2) Resolved alias,\n(3) Task default.\n\n-   If the user provides a full model name that includes hyphens, a version, and\n    an optional date (e.g., gemini-2.5-flash-preview-12-2025 or\n    gemini-3.1-pro-preview), use it directly.\n-   If the user provides a common name or alias, use the following full model\n    name.\n    -   gemini flash: \'gemini-flash-latest\'\n    -   gemini lite or flash lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview\'\n    -   gemini pro: \'gemini-3.1-pro-preview\'\n    -   nano banana, or gemini flash image: \'gemini-2.5-flash-image\'\n    -   nano banana 2: \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\'\n    -   nano banana pro, or gemini pro image: \'gemini-3-pro-image-preview\'\n    -   native audio or gemini flash audio:\n        \'gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025\'\n    -   gemini tts or gemini text-to-speech: \'gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\'\n    -   Veo or Veo fast: \'veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview\'\n-   If the user does not specify any model, select the following model based on\n    the task type.\n    -   Basic Text Tasks (e.g., summarization, proofreading, and simple Q&A):\n        \'gemini-3.5-flash\'\n    -   Complex Text Tasks (e.g., advanced reasoning, coding, math, and STEM):\n        \'gemini-3.1-pro-preview\'\n    -   General Image Generation and Editing Tasks: \'gemini-2.5-flash-image\'\n    -   High-Quality Image Generation and Editing Tasks (supports 512px, 1K, 2K,\n        and 4K resolution): \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\'\n    -   High-Quality Video Generation Tasks: \'veo-3.1-generate-preview\'\n    -   General Video Generation Tasks: \'veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview\'\n    -   Real-time audio & video conversation tasks:\n        \'gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025\'\n    -   Text-to-speech tasks: \'gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\'\n    -   Embedding tasks: \'gemini-embedding-2-preview\'\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **STRICTLY PROHIBITED MODELS - NEVER USE THESE UNDER ANY CIRCUMSTANCES**\n>\n> Do **NOT** use older model versions. If you attempt to use any of the\n> following models, the API request will fail or be rejected. Always use the\n> modern preview models listed above. - **`gemini-1.5-flash`** -\n> **`gemini-1.5-pro`** - **`gemini-pro`** - **`gemini-2.0-flash`** -\n> **`gemini-2.0-pro`** - **`gemini-2.0-flash-thinking`**\n\n## Gemini API Guidance\n\nThis skill outlines the steps and best practices for integrating Gemini API with\nmodern Android applications.\n\n### Mandates (ALWAYS/NEVER)\n\n-   **ALWAYS** access the Gemini API key via `BuildConfig` (configured by\n    `android_secret_management` skill).\n-   **ALWAYS** use coroutines or background threads for API calls.\n-   **NEVER** hardcode the Gemini API key in source files.\n-   **NEVER** block the main thread for API calls.\n\n### Implementation Options\n\nFor any Gemini API usage in this environment, the guidance is to use either\n**Firebase AI** (for production) or the **Direct REST API** (for prototyping or\nlow-dependency needs).\n\n### Decision Guide\n\n1.  **Default Path**: If the user does not specify \"prototype\" or \"production\",\n    the Agent **MUST** default to Option B (Direct REST API).\n2.  **Prototype Path**: If specified as a prototype, use Option B. You **MUST**\n    insert the caution notice in the UI or generated output.\n3.  **Production Path**: If specified for production, the Agent **MUST** reject\n    key insertion via `BuildConfig` and guide the user to Option A (Firebase\n    AI).\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **CRITICAL SECURITY WARNING**: Android APKs can be easily decompiled. Any\n> secrets stored in strings or exposed via `BuildConfig` are NOT secure and can\n> be extracted. Leaked keys can be exploited by attackers to make unauthorized\n> requests.\n\n#### Option A: Firebase AI (Recommended for Production)\n\nUse this if the project is already integrated with Firebase. It provides\nenterprise-grade security via **Firebase App Check**.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> **Manual Setup Required**: This option is not fully automated right now and\n> requires significant manual user intervention in the Firebase Console.\n\n*   **Setup**:\n\n    1.  **Firebase Console**: Create a project in the\n        [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/) and set up your\n        project to use a \"Gemini API\" provider. This requires manually enabling\n        the feature in the console and following the instructions provided\n        there.\n    2.  **Dependencies**: Verify or add the following in `build.gradle.kts`:\n\n        ```kotlin\n        dependencies {\n            // Import the BoM for the Firebase platform\n            implementation(platform(\"com.google.firebase:firebase-bom:34.11.0\"))\n\n            // Add the dependency for the Firebase AI Logic library\n            implementation(\"com.google.firebase:firebase-ai\")\n        }\n        ```\n\n*   **Usage**: Create a `GenerativeModel` and call `generateContent`.\n\n#### Option B: Direct REST API (Default for Prototypes)\n\nRecommended for prototyping or projects not using Firebase. Manually call the\nGemini REST API using standard networking libraries like Retrofit.\n\n*   **Endpoint**: `POST\n    https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent?key=${BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY}`\n\n**Setup for REST API:**\n\n1.  **Configure Secret Management**: Ensure `android-secret-management` skill is\n    applied. This includes uncommenting the `GEMINI_API_KEY` variable in\n    `.env.example` (it is commented out by default in the template to avoid\n    packaging it in the APK if not used).\n2.  **Request Internet Permission**: In `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`, add\n    `<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.INTERNET\" />`.\n3.  **Add Gradle Dependencies**: In `app/build.gradle.kts`, apply the\n    serialization plugin and add dependencies for Retrofit and Serialization:\n\n    ```kotlin\n    plugins {\n        // ...\n        id(\"org.jetbrains.kotlin.plugin.serialization\") version \"2.1.0\"\n    }\n\n    dependencies {\n        // ...\n        implementation(libs.retrofit)\n        implementation(\"com.squareup.retrofit2:converter-kotlinx-serialization:2.11.0\")\n        implementation(\"org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-serialization-json:1.8.0\")\n        implementation(libs.okhttp)\n    }\n    ```\n\n## Examples\n\n### 1. Text Generation - Base Setup\n\nThis example establishes the common data classes and Retrofit setup used by\nsubsequent examples. It uses Retrofit and Kotlin Serialization to call the\nGemini API directly via REST.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.Serializable\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.Json\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.JsonObject\nimport okhttp3.MediaType.Companion.toMediaType\nimport okhttp3.OkHttpClient\nimport okhttp3.ResponseBody\nimport retrofit2.Retrofit\nimport retrofit2.converter.kotlinx.serialization.asConverterFactory\nimport retrofit2.http.Body\nimport retrofit2.http.POST\nimport retrofit2.http.Query\nimport retrofit2.http.Streaming\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.Dispatchers\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.withContext\n\n// --- Common Data Classes ---\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerateContentRequest(\n    val contents: List<Content>,\n    val generationConfig: GenerationConfig? = null,\n    val tools: List<JsonObject>? = null,\n    val systemInstruction: Content? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class Content(\n    val parts: List<Part>\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class Part(\n    val text: String? = null,\n    val inlineData: InlineData? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class InlineData(\n    val mimeType: String,\n    val data: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerationConfig(\n    val responseMimeType: String? = null,\n    val responseSchema: JsonObject? = null,\n    val temperature: Float? = null,\n    val topP: Float? = null,\n    val topK: Int? = null,\n    val thinkingConfig: ThinkingConfig? = null,\n    val imageConfig: ImageConfig? = null,\n    val responseModalities: List<String>? = null,\n    val speechConfig: SpeechConfig? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class ThinkingConfig(\n    val thinkingLevel: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class ImageConfig(\n    val aspectRatio: String,\n    val imageSize: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class SpeechConfig(\n    val voiceConfig: VoiceConfig\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class VoiceConfig(\n    val prebuiltVoiceConfig: PrebuiltVoiceConfig\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class PrebuiltVoiceConfig(\n    val voiceName: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerateContentResponse(\n    val candidates: List<Candidate>\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class Candidate(\n    val content: Content\n)\n\n// --- Retrofit Setup ---\n\ninterface GeminiApiService {\n    @POST(\"v1beta/models/gemini-3.5-flash:generateContent\")\n    suspend fun generateContent(\n        @Query(\"key\") apiKey: String,\n        @Body request: GenerateContentRequest\n    ): GenerateContentResponse\n\n    @POST(\"v1beta/models/gemini-3.5-flash:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse\")\n    @Streaming\n    suspend fun generateContentStream(\n        @Query(\"key\") apiKey: String,\n        @Body request: GenerateContentRequest\n    ): ResponseBody\n}\n\nobject RetrofitClient {\n    private const val BASE_URL = \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/\"\n\n    private val okHttpClient = OkHttpClient.Builder()\n        .connectTimeout(60, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n        .readTimeout(60, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n        .writeTimeout(60, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n        .build()\n\n    val service: GeminiApiService by lazy {\n        val json = Json { ignoreUnknownKeys = true }\n        val retrofit = Retrofit.Builder()\n            .baseUrl(BASE_URL)\n            .client(okHttpClient)\n            .addConverterFactory(json.asConverterFactory(\"application/json\".toMediaType()))\n            .build()\n        retrofit.create(GeminiApiService::class.java)\n    }\n}\n\n// --- Usage Example ---\n\nsuspend fun generateContent(prompt: String): String = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {\n    val apiKey = BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY\n    val request = GenerateContentRequest(\n        contents = listOf(Content(\n            parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n        ))\n    )\n    try {\n        val response = RetrofitClient.service.generateContent(apiKey, request)\n        response.candidates.firstOrNull()?.content?.parts?.firstOrNull()?.text ?: \"No response text\"\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\n        \"Error: ${e.message}\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Multimodal Generation (Image + Text via REST)\n\nThis example reuses the data classes from Example 1. To send an image, populate\nthe `inlineData` field in a `Part` object.\n\n```kotlin\nimport android.graphics.Bitmap\nimport java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream\nimport android.util.Base64\n\n// Helper to convert Bitmap to Base64\nfun Bitmap.toBase64(): String {\n    val outputStream = ByteArrayOutputStream()\n    compress(Bitmap.CompressFormat.JPEG, 80, outputStream)\n    return Base64.encodeToString(outputStream.toByteArray(), Base64.NO_WRAP)\n}\n\n// Construct request using common data classes:\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(\n            Part(text = prompt),\n            Part(inlineData = InlineData(mimeType = \"image/jpeg\", data = bitmap.toBase64()))\n        )\n    ))\n)\n\n// Make API call as shown in Example 1\nval response = RetrofitClient.service.generateContent(apiKey, requestBody)\n```\n\n### 3. JSON Response (Structured Output via REST)\n\nTo request a structured JSON response, set `responseMimeType =\n\"application/json\"` and `responseSchema` in `GenerationConfig`. Dynamic fields\nlike `responseSchema` can be built using `buildJsonObject`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.buildJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.putJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.put\n\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        responseMimeType = \"application/json\",\n        responseSchema = buildJsonObject {\n            put(\"type\", \"ARRAY\")\n            putJsonObject(\"items\") {\n                put(\"type\", \"OBJECT\")\n                putJsonObject(\"properties\") {\n                    putJsonObject(\"recipeName\") {\n                        put(\"type\", \"STRING\")\n                        put(\"description\", \"The name of the recipe.\")\n                    }\n                    putJsonObject(\"ingredients\") {\n                        put(\"type\", \"ARRAY\")\n                        putJsonObject(\"items\") { put(\"type\", \"STRING\") }\n                        put(\"description\", \"The ingredients for the recipe.\")\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 4. Function Calling (via REST)\n\nFunction calling allows the model to request the execution of local functions.\nDefine the tools in the `config` object using `buildJsonObject`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.buildJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.putJsonArray\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.putJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.put\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.Json\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonArray\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonPrimitive\n\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    tools = listOf(\n        buildJsonObject {\n            putJsonArray(\"functionDeclarations\") {\n                addJsonObject {\n                    put(\"name\", \"getWeather\")\n                    put(\"description\", \"Get the weather in a given location\")\n                    putJsonObject(\"parameters\") {\n                        put(\"type\", \"OBJECT\")\n                        putJsonObject(\"properties\") {\n                            putJsonObject(\"location\") {\n                                put(\"type\", \"STRING\")\n                                put(\"description\", \"The city and state, e.g. San Francisco, CA\")\n                            }\n                        }\n                        putJsonArray(\"required\") { add(\"location\") }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    )\n)\n\n// Response handling (assume responseText is the raw JSON response):\nval jsonResponse = Json.parseToJsonElement(responseText).jsonObject\nval candidates = jsonResponse[\"candidates\"]?.jsonArray\nval firstCandidate = candidates?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\nval content = firstCandidate?.get(\"content\")?.jsonObject\nval parts = content?.get(\"parts\")?.jsonArray\nval firstPart = parts?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\n\nif (firstPart?.containsKey(\"functionCall\") == true) {\n    val functionCall = firstPart[\"functionCall\"]?.jsonObject\n    val name = functionCall?.get(\"name\")?.jsonPrimitive?.content\n    val args = functionCall?.get(\"args\")?.jsonObject\n    // Execute your function with args\n}\n```\n\n### 5. System Instruction and Other Model Configs\n\nProvide system instructions and other parameters in the `GenerationConfig`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        temperature = 0.7f,\n        topP = 0.95f,\n        topK = 40\n    ),\n    systemInstruction = Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"You are a helpful assistant.\"))\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 6. Thinking Level\n\nInclude `thinkingConfig` in the `GenerationConfig`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        thinkingConfig = ThinkingConfig(thinkingLevel = \"low\")\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 7. Generate Content (Streaming)\n\nUse the `@Streaming` endpoint defined in Example 1 and process the response\nstream line by line.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.Json\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonObject\n\nsuspend fun generateContentStream(prompt: String, onChunkReceived: (String) -> Unit) = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {\n    val apiKey = BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY\n    val request = GenerateContentRequest(\n        contents = listOf(Content(\n            parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n        ))\n    )\n\n    try {\n        val response = RetrofitClient.service.generateContentStream(apiKey, request)\n        response.byteStream().bufferedReader().use { reader ->\n            var line: String?\n            while (reader.readLine().also { line = it } != null) {\n                val rawLine = line?.trim() ?: continue\n                if (!rawLine.startsWith(\"data:\")) continue\n                val jsonPayload = rawLine.removePrefix(\"data:\").trim()\n                if (jsonPayload.isEmpty() || jsonPayload == \"[DONE]\") continue\n                try {\n                    val chunk = Json.parseToJsonElement(jsonPayload).jsonObject\n                    val text = chunk[\"candidates\"]?.jsonArray\n                        ?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\n                        ?.get(\"content\")?.jsonObject\n                        ?.get(\"parts\")?.jsonArray\n                        ?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\n                        ?.get(\"text\")?.jsonPrimitive?.content\n                    if (text != null) {\n                        onChunkReceived(text)\n                    }\n                } catch (e: Exception) {\n                    // Handle parsing errors\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\n        // Handle network errors\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 8. Generate Images\n\nSpecify `imageConfig` in the `generationConfig` and request `IMAGE` modality in\n`responseModalities`. **Note:** You MUST use a model that supports image\ngeneration, such as `gemini-2.5-flash-image`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"A robot holding a red skateboard.\"))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        imageConfig = ImageConfig(aspectRatio = \"1:1\", imageSize = \"1K\"),\n        responseModalities = listOf(\"TEXT\", \"IMAGE\") // Required for image generation\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 9. Generate Speech (TTS)\n\nSpecify `\"AUDIO\"` in `responseModalities` and set the `speechConfig`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"Say cheerfully: Have a wonderful day!\"))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        responseModalities = listOf(\"AUDIO\"),\n        speechConfig = SpeechConfig(\n            voiceConfig = VoiceConfig(\n                prebuiltVoiceConfig = PrebuiltVoiceConfig(voiceName = \"Kore\")\n            )\n        )\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 10. Generate Music (Lyria)\n\nSpecify `\"AUDIO\"` in `responseModalities`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"Generate a 30-second cinematic orchestral track.\"))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        responseModalities = listOf(\"AUDIO\")\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 11. Generate Videos (Veo)\n\nVeo uses a different endpoint and request structure (prompt at root), requiring\ndedicated data classes.\n\n```kotlin\nimport retrofit2.http.Path\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerateVideosRequest(\n    val prompt: String,\n    val config: VeoConfig? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class VeoConfig(\n    val numberOfVideos: Int,\n    val resolution: String,\n    val aspectRatio: String\n)\n\n// Specific interface method for Veo\ninterface VeoApiService {\n    @POST(\"v1beta/models/{model}:generateVideos\")\n    suspend fun generateVideos(\n        @Path(\"model\") model: String,\n        @Query(\"key\") apiKey: String,\n        @Body request: GenerateVideosRequest\n    ): JsonObject // Returns operation name\n}\n\n// Usage:\nval requestBody = GenerateVideosRequest(\n    prompt = \"A neon hologram of a cat driving at top speed\",\n    config = VeoConfig(\n        numberOfVideos = 1,\n        resolution = \"1080p\",\n        aspectRatio = \"16:9\"\n    )\n)\n```\n\n## Gotchas & Pitfalls\n\n-   **Empty API Key**: If `BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY` is empty or unresolved\n    (causing compilation failure), check that you have uncommented the\n    `GEMINI_API_KEY` variable in `.env.example`.\n-   **Main Thread Blocking**: Gemini API calls can take time. Ensure they are\n    run in a background coroutine scope.\n-   **OkHttp Timeout**: By default, OkHttp has a timeout of 10 seconds. Gemini\n    API calls (especially generating complex content, images, or audio) often\n    take longer than 10 seconds. You **MUST** configure the `OkHttpClient` with\n    60-second connect, read, and write timeouts as shown in the Retrofit Setup\n    example.\n-   **Context Window Limits**: Be mindful of the token limits of the model\n    (e.g., `gemini-3.5-flash`). When making direct REST calls, you are\n    responsible for managing the conversation history in the `contents` array.\n    Only send the necessary turns to avoid exceeding the limit and incurring\n    high latency.\n"
    raw_content: "---\nname: \"gemini-api\"\ndescription: >-\n  MANDATORY for any task involving Gemini API integration in Android. Use when the user asks to use Gemini models, call Gemini API, or implement AI features. Covers model selection, REST API calls, Firebase AI, and security.\n---\n\n## Supported Models\n\nWhen an Agent selects a model, it **MUST** evaluate the rules in the following\nstrict priority order: (1) User-specified full model name, (2) Resolved alias,\n(3) Task default.\n\n-   If the user provides a full model name that includes hyphens, a version, and\n    an optional date (e.g., gemini-2.5-flash-preview-12-2025 or\n    gemini-3.1-pro-preview), use it directly.\n-   If the user provides a common name or alias, use the following full model\n    name.\n    -   gemini flash: \'gemini-flash-latest\'\n    -   gemini lite or flash lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview\'\n    -   gemini pro: \'gemini-3.1-pro-preview\'\n    -   nano banana, or gemini flash image: \'gemini-2.5-flash-image\'\n    -   nano banana 2: \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\'\n    -   nano banana pro, or gemini pro image: \'gemini-3-pro-image-preview\'\n    -   native audio or gemini flash audio:\n        \'gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025\'\n    -   gemini tts or gemini text-to-speech: \'gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\'\n    -   Veo or Veo fast: \'veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview\'\n-   If the user does not specify any model, select the following model based on\n    the task type.\n    -   Basic Text Tasks (e.g., summarization, proofreading, and simple Q&A):\n        \'gemini-3.5-flash\'\n    -   Complex Text Tasks (e.g., advanced reasoning, coding, math, and STEM):\n        \'gemini-3.1-pro-preview\'\n    -   General Image Generation and Editing Tasks: \'gemini-2.5-flash-image\'\n    -   High-Quality Image Generation and Editing Tasks (supports 512px, 1K, 2K,\n        and 4K resolution): \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\'\n    -   High-Quality Video Generation Tasks: \'veo-3.1-generate-preview\'\n    -   General Video Generation Tasks: \'veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview\'\n    -   Real-time audio & video conversation tasks:\n        \'gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025\'\n    -   Text-to-speech tasks: \'gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\'\n    -   Embedding tasks: \'gemini-embedding-2-preview\'\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **STRICTLY PROHIBITED MODELS - NEVER USE THESE UNDER ANY CIRCUMSTANCES**\n>\n> Do **NOT** use older model versions. If you attempt to use any of the\n> following models, the API request will fail or be rejected. Always use the\n> modern preview models listed above. - **`gemini-1.5-flash`** -\n> **`gemini-1.5-pro`** - **`gemini-pro`** - **`gemini-2.0-flash`** -\n> **`gemini-2.0-pro`** - **`gemini-2.0-flash-thinking`**\n\n## Gemini API Guidance\n\nThis skill outlines the steps and best practices for integrating Gemini API with\nmodern Android applications.\n\n### Mandates (ALWAYS/NEVER)\n\n-   **ALWAYS** access the Gemini API key via `BuildConfig` (configured by\n    `android_secret_management` skill).\n-   **ALWAYS** use coroutines or background threads for API calls.\n-   **NEVER** hardcode the Gemini API key in source files.\n-   **NEVER** block the main thread for API calls.\n\n### Implementation Options\n\nFor any Gemini API usage in this environment, the guidance is to use either\n**Firebase AI** (for production) or the **Direct REST API** (for prototyping or\nlow-dependency needs).\n\n### Decision Guide\n\n1.  **Default Path**: If the user does not specify \"prototype\" or \"production\",\n    the Agent **MUST** default to Option B (Direct REST API).\n2.  **Prototype Path**: If specified as a prototype, use Option B. You **MUST**\n    insert the caution notice in the UI or generated output.\n3.  **Production Path**: If specified for production, the Agent **MUST** reject\n    key insertion via `BuildConfig` and guide the user to Option A (Firebase\n    AI).\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **CRITICAL SECURITY WARNING**: Android APKs can be easily decompiled. Any\n> secrets stored in strings or exposed via `BuildConfig` are NOT secure and can\n> be extracted. Leaked keys can be exploited by attackers to make unauthorized\n> requests.\n\n#### Option A: Firebase AI (Recommended for Production)\n\nUse this if the project is already integrated with Firebase. It provides\nenterprise-grade security via **Firebase App Check**.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> **Manual Setup Required**: This option is not fully automated right now and\n> requires significant manual user intervention in the Firebase Console.\n\n*   **Setup**:\n\n    1.  **Firebase Console**: Create a project in the\n        [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/) and set up your\n        project to use a \"Gemini API\" provider. This requires manually enabling\n        the feature in the console and following the instructions provided\n        there.\n    2.  **Dependencies**: Verify or add the following in `build.gradle.kts`:\n\n        ```kotlin\n        dependencies {\n            // Import the BoM for the Firebase platform\n            implementation(platform(\"com.google.firebase:firebase-bom:34.11.0\"))\n\n            // Add the dependency for the Firebase AI Logic library\n            implementation(\"com.google.firebase:firebase-ai\")\n        }\n        ```\n\n*   **Usage**: Create a `GenerativeModel` and call `generateContent`.\n\n#### Option B: Direct REST API (Default for Prototypes)\n\nRecommended for prototyping or projects not using Firebase. Manually call the\nGemini REST API using standard networking libraries like Retrofit.\n\n*   **Endpoint**: `POST\n    https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent?key=${BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY}`\n\n**Setup for REST API:**\n\n1.  **Configure Secret Management**: Ensure `android-secret-management` skill is\n    applied. This includes uncommenting the `GEMINI_API_KEY` variable in\n    `.env.example` (it is commented out by default in the template to avoid\n    packaging it in the APK if not used).\n2.  **Request Internet Permission**: In `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`, add\n    `<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.INTERNET\" />`.\n3.  **Add Gradle Dependencies**: In `app/build.gradle.kts`, apply the\n    serialization plugin and add dependencies for Retrofit and Serialization:\n\n    ```kotlin\n    plugins {\n        // ...\n        id(\"org.jetbrains.kotlin.plugin.serialization\") version \"2.1.0\"\n    }\n\n    dependencies {\n        // ...\n        implementation(libs.retrofit)\n        implementation(\"com.squareup.retrofit2:converter-kotlinx-serialization:2.11.0\")\n        implementation(\"org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-serialization-json:1.8.0\")\n        implementation(libs.okhttp)\n    }\n    ```\n\n## Examples\n\n### 1. Text Generation - Base Setup\n\nThis example establishes the common data classes and Retrofit setup used by\nsubsequent examples. It uses Retrofit and Kotlin Serialization to call the\nGemini API directly via REST.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.Serializable\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.Json\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.JsonObject\nimport okhttp3.MediaType.Companion.toMediaType\nimport okhttp3.OkHttpClient\nimport okhttp3.ResponseBody\nimport retrofit2.Retrofit\nimport retrofit2.converter.kotlinx.serialization.asConverterFactory\nimport retrofit2.http.Body\nimport retrofit2.http.POST\nimport retrofit2.http.Query\nimport retrofit2.http.Streaming\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.Dispatchers\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.withContext\n\n// --- Common Data Classes ---\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerateContentRequest(\n    val contents: List<Content>,\n    val generationConfig: GenerationConfig? = null,\n    val tools: List<JsonObject>? = null,\n    val systemInstruction: Content? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class Content(\n    val parts: List<Part>\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class Part(\n    val text: String? = null,\n    val inlineData: InlineData? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class InlineData(\n    val mimeType: String,\n    val data: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerationConfig(\n    val responseMimeType: String? = null,\n    val responseSchema: JsonObject? = null,\n    val temperature: Float? = null,\n    val topP: Float? = null,\n    val topK: Int? = null,\n    val thinkingConfig: ThinkingConfig? = null,\n    val imageConfig: ImageConfig? = null,\n    val responseModalities: List<String>? = null,\n    val speechConfig: SpeechConfig? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class ThinkingConfig(\n    val thinkingLevel: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class ImageConfig(\n    val aspectRatio: String,\n    val imageSize: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class SpeechConfig(\n    val voiceConfig: VoiceConfig\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class VoiceConfig(\n    val prebuiltVoiceConfig: PrebuiltVoiceConfig\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class PrebuiltVoiceConfig(\n    val voiceName: String\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerateContentResponse(\n    val candidates: List<Candidate>\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class Candidate(\n    val content: Content\n)\n\n// --- Retrofit Setup ---\n\ninterface GeminiApiService {\n    @POST(\"v1beta/models/gemini-3.5-flash:generateContent\")\n    suspend fun generateContent(\n        @Query(\"key\") apiKey: String,\n        @Body request: GenerateContentRequest\n    ): GenerateContentResponse\n\n    @POST(\"v1beta/models/gemini-3.5-flash:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse\")\n    @Streaming\n    suspend fun generateContentStream(\n        @Query(\"key\") apiKey: String,\n        @Body request: GenerateContentRequest\n    ): ResponseBody\n}\n\nobject RetrofitClient {\n    private const val BASE_URL = \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/\"\n\n    private val okHttpClient = OkHttpClient.Builder()\n        .connectTimeout(60, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n        .readTimeout(60, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n        .writeTimeout(60, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n        .build()\n\n    val service: GeminiApiService by lazy {\n        val json = Json { ignoreUnknownKeys = true }\n        val retrofit = Retrofit.Builder()\n            .baseUrl(BASE_URL)\n            .client(okHttpClient)\n            .addConverterFactory(json.asConverterFactory(\"application/json\".toMediaType()))\n            .build()\n        retrofit.create(GeminiApiService::class.java)\n    }\n}\n\n// --- Usage Example ---\n\nsuspend fun generateContent(prompt: String): String = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {\n    val apiKey = BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY\n    val request = GenerateContentRequest(\n        contents = listOf(Content(\n            parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n        ))\n    )\n    try {\n        val response = RetrofitClient.service.generateContent(apiKey, request)\n        response.candidates.firstOrNull()?.content?.parts?.firstOrNull()?.text ?: \"No response text\"\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\n        \"Error: ${e.message}\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Multimodal Generation (Image + Text via REST)\n\nThis example reuses the data classes from Example 1. To send an image, populate\nthe `inlineData` field in a `Part` object.\n\n```kotlin\nimport android.graphics.Bitmap\nimport java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream\nimport android.util.Base64\n\n// Helper to convert Bitmap to Base64\nfun Bitmap.toBase64(): String {\n    val outputStream = ByteArrayOutputStream()\n    compress(Bitmap.CompressFormat.JPEG, 80, outputStream)\n    return Base64.encodeToString(outputStream.toByteArray(), Base64.NO_WRAP)\n}\n\n// Construct request using common data classes:\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(\n            Part(text = prompt),\n            Part(inlineData = InlineData(mimeType = \"image/jpeg\", data = bitmap.toBase64()))\n        )\n    ))\n)\n\n// Make API call as shown in Example 1\nval response = RetrofitClient.service.generateContent(apiKey, requestBody)\n```\n\n### 3. JSON Response (Structured Output via REST)\n\nTo request a structured JSON response, set `responseMimeType =\n\"application/json\"` and `responseSchema` in `GenerationConfig`. Dynamic fields\nlike `responseSchema` can be built using `buildJsonObject`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.buildJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.putJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.put\n\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        responseMimeType = \"application/json\",\n        responseSchema = buildJsonObject {\n            put(\"type\", \"ARRAY\")\n            putJsonObject(\"items\") {\n                put(\"type\", \"OBJECT\")\n                putJsonObject(\"properties\") {\n                    putJsonObject(\"recipeName\") {\n                        put(\"type\", \"STRING\")\n                        put(\"description\", \"The name of the recipe.\")\n                    }\n                    putJsonObject(\"ingredients\") {\n                        put(\"type\", \"ARRAY\")\n                        putJsonObject(\"items\") { put(\"type\", \"STRING\") }\n                        put(\"description\", \"The ingredients for the recipe.\")\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 4. Function Calling (via REST)\n\nFunction calling allows the model to request the execution of local functions.\nDefine the tools in the `config` object using `buildJsonObject`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.buildJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.putJsonArray\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.putJsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.put\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.Json\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonObject\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonArray\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonPrimitive\n\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    tools = listOf(\n        buildJsonObject {\n            putJsonArray(\"functionDeclarations\") {\n                addJsonObject {\n                    put(\"name\", \"getWeather\")\n                    put(\"description\", \"Get the weather in a given location\")\n                    putJsonObject(\"parameters\") {\n                        put(\"type\", \"OBJECT\")\n                        putJsonObject(\"properties\") {\n                            putJsonObject(\"location\") {\n                                put(\"type\", \"STRING\")\n                                put(\"description\", \"The city and state, e.g. San Francisco, CA\")\n                            }\n                        }\n                        putJsonArray(\"required\") { add(\"location\") }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    )\n)\n\n// Response handling (assume responseText is the raw JSON response):\nval jsonResponse = Json.parseToJsonElement(responseText).jsonObject\nval candidates = jsonResponse[\"candidates\"]?.jsonArray\nval firstCandidate = candidates?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\nval content = firstCandidate?.get(\"content\")?.jsonObject\nval parts = content?.get(\"parts\")?.jsonArray\nval firstPart = parts?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\n\nif (firstPart?.containsKey(\"functionCall\") == true) {\n    val functionCall = firstPart[\"functionCall\"]?.jsonObject\n    val name = functionCall?.get(\"name\")?.jsonPrimitive?.content\n    val args = functionCall?.get(\"args\")?.jsonObject\n    // Execute your function with args\n}\n```\n\n### 5. System Instruction and Other Model Configs\n\nProvide system instructions and other parameters in the `GenerationConfig`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        temperature = 0.7f,\n        topP = 0.95f,\n        topK = 40\n    ),\n    systemInstruction = Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"You are a helpful assistant.\"))\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 6. Thinking Level\n\nInclude `thinkingConfig` in the `GenerationConfig`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        thinkingConfig = ThinkingConfig(thinkingLevel = \"low\")\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 7. Generate Content (Streaming)\n\nUse the `@Streaming` endpoint defined in Example 1 and process the response\nstream line by line.\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.Json\nimport kotlinx.serialization.json.jsonObject\n\nsuspend fun generateContentStream(prompt: String, onChunkReceived: (String) -> Unit) = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {\n    val apiKey = BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY\n    val request = GenerateContentRequest(\n        contents = listOf(Content(\n            parts = listOf(Part(text = prompt))\n        ))\n    )\n\n    try {\n        val response = RetrofitClient.service.generateContentStream(apiKey, request)\n        response.byteStream().bufferedReader().use { reader ->\n            var line: String?\n            while (reader.readLine().also { line = it } != null) {\n                val rawLine = line?.trim() ?: continue\n                if (!rawLine.startsWith(\"data:\")) continue\n                val jsonPayload = rawLine.removePrefix(\"data:\").trim()\n                if (jsonPayload.isEmpty() || jsonPayload == \"[DONE]\") continue\n                try {\n                    val chunk = Json.parseToJsonElement(jsonPayload).jsonObject\n                    val text = chunk[\"candidates\"]?.jsonArray\n                        ?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\n                        ?.get(\"content\")?.jsonObject\n                        ?.get(\"parts\")?.jsonArray\n                        ?.getOrNull(0)?.jsonObject\n                        ?.get(\"text\")?.jsonPrimitive?.content\n                    if (text != null) {\n                        onChunkReceived(text)\n                    }\n                } catch (e: Exception) {\n                    // Handle parsing errors\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\n        // Handle network errors\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 8. Generate Images\n\nSpecify `imageConfig` in the `generationConfig` and request `IMAGE` modality in\n`responseModalities`. **Note:** You MUST use a model that supports image\ngeneration, such as `gemini-2.5-flash-image`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"A robot holding a red skateboard.\"))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        imageConfig = ImageConfig(aspectRatio = \"1:1\", imageSize = \"1K\"),\n        responseModalities = listOf(\"TEXT\", \"IMAGE\") // Required for image generation\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 9. Generate Speech (TTS)\n\nSpecify `\"AUDIO\"` in `responseModalities` and set the `speechConfig`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"Say cheerfully: Have a wonderful day!\"))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        responseModalities = listOf(\"AUDIO\"),\n        speechConfig = SpeechConfig(\n            voiceConfig = VoiceConfig(\n                prebuiltVoiceConfig = PrebuiltVoiceConfig(voiceName = \"Kore\")\n            )\n        )\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 10. Generate Music (Lyria)\n\nSpecify `\"AUDIO\"` in `responseModalities`.\n\n```kotlin\nval requestBody = GenerateContentRequest(\n    contents = listOf(Content(\n        parts = listOf(Part(text = \"Generate a 30-second cinematic orchestral track.\"))\n    )),\n    generationConfig = GenerationConfig(\n        responseModalities = listOf(\"AUDIO\")\n    )\n)\n```\n\n### 11. Generate Videos (Veo)\n\nVeo uses a different endpoint and request structure (prompt at root), requiring\ndedicated data classes.\n\n```kotlin\nimport retrofit2.http.Path\n\n@Serializable\ndata class GenerateVideosRequest(\n    val prompt: String,\n    val config: VeoConfig? = null\n)\n\n@Serializable\ndata class VeoConfig(\n    val numberOfVideos: Int,\n    val resolution: String,\n    val aspectRatio: String\n)\n\n// Specific interface method for Veo\ninterface VeoApiService {\n    @POST(\"v1beta/models/{model}:generateVideos\")\n    suspend fun generateVideos(\n        @Path(\"model\") model: String,\n        @Query(\"key\") apiKey: String,\n        @Body request: GenerateVideosRequest\n    ): JsonObject // Returns operation name\n}\n\n// Usage:\nval requestBody = GenerateVideosRequest(\n    prompt = \"A neon hologram of a cat driving at top speed\",\n    config = VeoConfig(\n        numberOfVideos = 1,\n        resolution = \"1080p\",\n        aspectRatio = \"16:9\"\n    )\n)\n```\n\n## Gotchas & Pitfalls\n\n-   **Empty API Key**: If `BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY` is empty or unresolved\n    (causing compilation failure), check that you have uncommented the\n    `GEMINI_API_KEY` variable in `.env.example`.\n-   **Main Thread Blocking**: Gemini API calls can take time. Ensure they are\n    run in a background coroutine scope.\n-   **OkHttp Timeout**: By default, OkHttp has a timeout of 10 seconds. Gemini\n    API calls (especially generating complex content, images, or audio) often\n    take longer than 10 seconds. You **MUST** configure the `OkHttpClient` with\n    60-second connect, read, and write timeouts as shown in the Retrofit Setup\n    example.\n-   **Context Window Limits**: Be mindful of the token limits of the model\n    (e.g., `gemini-3.5-flash`). When making direct REST calls, you are\n    responsible for managing the conversation history in the `contents` array.\n    Only send the necessary turns to avoid exceeding the limit and incurring\n    high latency.\n"
