    thinking: "**Analyzing the Project\'s Scope**\n\nI\'m diving into the user\'s detailed specifications for this document scanner. Right now, I\'m carefully reviewing the architectural and feature requirements, specifically focusing on the core domains \342\200\223 Documents, Pages, and Scans. I\'m aiming to understand the scope and complexity before moving on to the more granular aspects.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Parameters**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the project\'s features. Specifically, I am focusing on the user\'s defined categories/types, the folders, tags, signatures, annotations, OCR results, and quality metrics that define the project scope. Right now I am trying to understand the image processing and core camera pipeline requirements, including the auto-detection, and various mode selectors like the single or multi-page mode.\n\n\n**Detailing UI Specifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user interface elements. I\'m focusing on the corner crop screen with its draggable handles, and loupe. Then, the document enhancement filters, which include options for original, \"magic,\" \"document,\" black & white, grayscale, and color boost. I am also investigating the document quality analyzer and its metrics. Finally, I\'m examining the multipage features like a real-time thumbnail tray and page manager for reordering, adding, deleting, retaking and rotating the images.\n\n\n**Outlining OCR Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the OCR and Document AI features. I\'m prioritizing the dual-mode OCR approach, specifically the fast offline and deep Gemini AI options. I\'m detailing the interactive viewer, including its search, edit, and export functions. Additionally, I am clarifying the searchable PDF generation with a text layer. The goal is to provide a complete document management experience.\n\n\n\n**Clarifying Security Features**\n\nI am now focusing on security features, and I\'m detailing the encryption flags to be employed. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of a searchable text layer embedded in PDFs. I\'m now also detailing the new PDF annotation tools and electronic signature tools. They include a drawing canvas, and smart redaction features. Finally, I\'m examining the Document Library and File Manager with features like view modes, organization through folders, tags, favorites, and a trash bin with restore and empty functions, and a comprehensive global search capability.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Priorities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interactions and data management. I\'ve detailed the document search functionality, including full OCR text content and filtering options. I\'m also specifying the storage manager features and have added details for import and export functions, including photo picker and export formats. I\'m further clarifying privacy and security measures, emphasizing the offline-first design and app lock capabilities. Premium UX/UI features are being refined with material 3 design, including the emerald/teal and deep slate styling, and RTL localization.\n\n\n"
