  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "This summary establishes the foundation for the development of \"DocScan Pro,\" a premium-grade document scanner application.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Full Product & Technical Implementation:** The user has provided a comprehensive 54-point requirement list for a professional document scanner. We have completed the audit and initial setup. The project is now ready to begin the implementation phases.\n    *   **Status:** PLANNING / TRANSITIONING TO IMPLEMENTATION.\n*   **Phase 3: Core Scanner Engine:** The next immediate technical goal is to implement the Camera Scanner Engine, specifically focusing on Automatic Document Detection and Smart Auto Capture.\n    *   **Status:** NOT STARTED.\n*   **Ongoing Requirements:** The entire 54-point requirement list (covering OCR, PDF generation, Document Library, Privacy, etc.) remains the active backlog for the project.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Preferences & Rules:**\n    *   \"I want a **premium, modern, professional, minimal, elegant, fast, and trustworthy** product.\"\n    *   \"No \'fake features.\' Every button must be functional, connected, and tested.\"\n    *   \"Privacy is a key feature. Data must remain local by default.\"\n    *   \"Arabic must be supported excellently (RTL, connected text, Arabic/English mixed documents).\"\n    *   \"Offline-first: The core scanner must not require internet.\"\n    *   \"Architecture: Clean Architecture, Dependency Injection, Repository Pattern, Modular Services.\"\n*   **Design Direction:** Avoid generic AI defaults. Use asymmetry, depth, and intentional visual hierarchy.\n*   **Scope:** The user explicitly stated: \"I want a real, long-term commercial product, not a prototype or demo.\"\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **Product & Technical Audit:** Completed the full analysis of the 54-point requirement list, establishing the architectural approach and defining the development phases (PHASE 1 & 2 complete).\n*   **Project Setup:**\n    *   Updated `metadata.json` with the app name \"DocScan Pro\" and a professional description.\n    *   Updated `settings.gradle.kts` to set the `rootProject.name` to \"DocScan Pro\".\n    *   **Branding:** Created a custom adaptive app icon.\n        *   *Background:* Custom modern gradient (`#0F172A` to `#0F2942`) with subtle grid accents.\n        *   *Foreground:* Custom vector silhouette representing a document with a laser scan beam and corner crop brackets.\n*   **Verification:** Confirmed the base project compiles successfully.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture:** The project follows a strict layered architecture: UI Layer \342\206\222 Application Layer \342\206\222 Domain Layer \342\206\222 Infrastructure (Storage/Camera/OCR/PDF).\n*   **Dependencies:** The project is configured with `libs.versions.toml` using `Room` for persistence, `CameraX` (via `androidx.camera` libraries), `Retrofit` for networking, and `Compose` for UI.\n*   **Failures:** The `generate_image` tool failed due to resource exhaustion (usage limit). The icon was created manually via vector drawable code.\n*   **Constraints:**\n    *   API keys must be handled via `BuildConfig` and secret management (not hardcoded).\n    *   All database operations must use `suspend` functions or `Flow` and be accessed via the Repository pattern.\n    *   Must use `ksp` for Room code generation.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml`: Created custom modern gradient background.\n    *   `/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml`: Created custom vector scanner icon.\n    *   `/metadata.json`: Updated with app name and description.\n    *   `/settings.gradle.kts`: Updated project name.\n*   **Viewed Files (Relevant for next steps):**\n    *   `/app/build.gradle.kts`: Contains dependency definitions and build configurations.\n    *   `/gradle/libs.versions.toml`: Centralized dependency versions.\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/room_database_integration/SKILL.md`: Guidelines for Room implementation.\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/design_guidelines/SKILL.md`: Guidelines for M3/Compose styling.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Immediate Next Step:** Begin **PHASE 3: Core Scanner Engine**.\n*   **Action Plan:**\n    1.  Implement the CameraX integration in `MainActivity` or a dedicated `ScannerScreen`.\n    2.  Set up the `CameraProvider` and `ImageCapture` use cases.\n    3.  Implement the `PreviewView` for the camera feed.\n    4.  Ensure proper permission handling (Camera, Storage) as per the user\'s requirement for \"smart permission management.\"\n*   **Relevant Skills to re-read:**\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/design_guidelines/SKILL.md` (for UI implementation).\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/room_database_integration/SKILL.md` (for data persistence).\n*   **User Quote:** \"The camera is the heart of the application. Do not make the experience just a normal photo capture... Create a smart scanner engine.\""
