    thinking: "**Defining UI Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently structuring the UI using Material 3, focusing on clean navigation routes. I\'ve defined core routes like HOME, SCAN, VIEWER, and various routes for image manipulation and export, including CROP, FILTER, OCR, ANNOTATE and STORAGE. I\'m aiming for high aesthetic polish throughout the user interface.\n\n\n**Detailing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously designing the UI components. I\'ve got a top bar and document card looking sleek. Also, I\342\200\231ve made category chips that can filter fast, and a magnifier loupe that previews corners being dragged. I\'ve crafted a sophisticated scanner overlay, and finally, a secure PIN entry keypad.\n\n\n**Refining Scanner Interface**\n\nI\'m now detailing the scanner interface. I\'m focusing on real-time edge detection and a corner quad overlay using `ImageAnalysis`. I\'m working on the auto-capture logic, including a countdown circle, mode selector tabs for different scan types, and flash and grid toggles. I\'ve also incorporated a gallery import button and a live page tray.\n\n\n"
