    session_summary: "This summary provides the current state of the \"DocScan Pro\" project. The core architectural and engine layers have been implemented, and the project is ready for UI screen integration and refinement.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Full Product & Technical Implementation:** Build a professional, premium-grade document scanner application.\n    *   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION (Transitioning from Core Engine to UI Integration).\n*   **Core Scanner Engine:** Implement the CameraX integration within the `CameraScanScreen` to utilize the `ScannerOverlay` and `ScanViewModel`.\n    *   **Status:** NOT STARTED.\n*   **Document Viewer & Editor:** Implement the UI for viewing, cropping, filtering, and annotating documents.\n    *   **Status:** NOT STARTED.\n*   **Privacy & Security:** Implement the PIN lock mechanism using the existing `PinLockDialog` component.\n    *   **Status:** NOT STARTED.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Preferences & Rules:**\n    *   \"I want a **premium, modern, professional, minimal, elegant, fast, and trustworthy** product.\"\n    *   \"No \'fake features.\' Every button must be functional, connected, and tested.\"\n    *   \"Privacy is a key feature. Data must remain local by default.\"\n    *   \"Arabic must be supported excellently (RTL, connected text, Arabic/English mixed documents).\"\n    *   \"Offline-first: The core scanner must not require internet.\"\n    *   \"Architecture: Clean Architecture, Dependency Injection, Repository Pattern, Modular Services.\"\n*   **Design Direction:** Avoid generic AI defaults. Use asymmetry, depth, and intentional visual hierarchy.\n*   **Scope:** \"I want a real, long-term commercial product, not a prototype or demo.\"\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **Project Infrastructure:** Configured `build.gradle.kts` with necessary dependencies (CameraX, Room, Coil, Navigation), updated `AndroidManifest.xml` with permissions and `FileProvider`, and created `file_paths.xml`.\n*   **Theming:** Implemented a custom Emerald/Slate/Pearl color palette in `Color.kt` and `Theme.kt`.\n*   **Data Layer:** Implemented Room entities (`DocumentEntity`, `PageEntity`, `SignatureEntity`), `DocumentDao`, and `DocumentRepository` to handle transactional data operations.\n*   **Engine Layer:**\n    *   **CV:** Created `ImageProcessor` (perspective warping, filters, quality analysis) and `DocumentDetector` (real-time boundary detection).\n    *   **OCR:** Created `DocumentAiEngine` (offline heuristic OCR + Gemini 2.5 Flash integration).\n    *   **PDF:** Created `PdfEngine` for multi-page searchable PDF generation.\n    *   **Annotation:** Created `AnnotationEngine` for burning pen/highlighter/signature/redaction layers into images.\n*   **UI Components:** Created reusable components: `ScannerOverlay`, `CornerMagnifierLoupe`, `DocumentCard`, `CategoryChipsRow`, and `PinLockDialog`.\n*   **Screens:** Created `HomeScreen` with search, filtering, and trash bin management.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture:** The app follows a strict layered architecture: `UI Layer` (Compose) -> `ViewModel` -> `Repository` -> `Engine/Database`.\n*   **Concurrency:** All database and I/O operations are performed using `suspend` functions and `Dispatchers.IO` within the Repository and ViewModels.\n*   **CV/Detection:** The `DocumentDetector` uses a downsampled frame analysis approach to maintain high performance during real-time preview.\n*   **OCR:** The `DocumentAiEngine` is designed as a hybrid system: it falls back to offline heuristic extraction if the Gemini API key is missing or the network fails.\n*   **Constraints:**\n    *   API keys must be handled via `BuildConfig` (injected by AI Studio).\n    *   All file operations use `FileProvider` for secure sharing.\n    *   The project is configured for `ksp` and Room code generation.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/.env.example`: Enabled `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n    *   `/app/build.gradle.kts`: Configured dependencies and `applicationId`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`: Added permissions, `FileProvider`, and `windowSoftInputMode`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml` & `/values-ar/strings.xml`: Added full UI string resources (English/Arabic).\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/theme/`: Created `Color.kt` and `Theme.kt`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/`: Created `DocumentCategory.kt`, `DocumentEntity.kt`, `DocumentDao.kt`, `DocScanDatabase.kt`, `DocumentRepository.kt`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/engine/`: Created `DocumentQuad.kt`, `ImageProcessor.kt`, `DocumentDetector.kt`, `DocumentAiEngine.kt`, `PdfEngine.kt`, `AnnotationEngine.kt`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/viewmodel/`: Created `ScanViewModel.kt`, `DocumentViewModel.kt`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/`: Created `ScannerOverlay.kt`, `CornerMagnifierLoupe.kt`, `DocumentCard.kt`, `CategoryChipsRow.kt`, `PinLockDialog.kt`.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/home/HomeScreen.kt`: Created main dashboard.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/gradle/libs.versions.toml`: Referenced for dependency management.\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/design_guidelines/SKILL.md`: Used for M3/Compose styling.\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/room_database_integration/SKILL.md`: Used for Room implementation.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Current State:** The project is fully architected with core engines and basic UI components ready.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    1.  **Integrate CameraX:** Implement `CameraScanScreen` using `CameraX` (Preview, ImageCapture, ImageAnalysis). The `ImageAnalysis` use case should feed frames into `ScanViewModel.onFrameAnalyzed`.\n    2.  **Navigation:** Implement the `NavHost` in `MainActivity` to connect `HomeScreen` to `CameraScanScreen` and `DocumentViewer`.\n    3.  **Document Viewer:** Implement the UI for the document viewer screen, allowing users to view pages, apply filters, and trigger OCR.\n    4.  **Refinement:** Apply the defined theme and polish the UI components.\n\n*   **Relevant Skills to re-read:**\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/design_guidelines/SKILL.md` (for UI implementation).\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/room_database_integration/SKILL.md` (for data persistence)."
    included_step_index_start: 41
    included_step_index_end: 110
